-- chem/pairlevel.cub — the two-electron singlet ground level from below with no spectral hypothesis, the repulsion's
-- strength a parameter (docs/chemical-identity.md, "The lower bound is one square over a solved base", (b)).
-- The operator is H_g = −½∇₁² − ½∇₂² − 2/r₁ − 2/r₂ + g/r₁₂, g a positive rational. With lengths scaled by 2/ζ the
-- two-electron ion at charge ζ is (ζ/2)²·H_g at g = 2/ζ: helium is g = 1, lithium's pair (charge 3/2) is g = 4/3
-- (the scaling is taken). On a Hylleraas span (chem/he.cub's φ_ijk at one exponent α) the three matrices are
--   S = ⟨φ, φ⟩ (`he-sel`),   Hm(g) = ⟨φ, H_g φ⟩ = he-hel + (g − 1)·⟨φ, r₁₂⁻¹ φ⟩ (`pl-hm`),
--   H2(g) = ⟨H_g φ, H_g φ⟩ (`pl-hh`): chem/he2.cub's monomials of Hφ with (g − 1)/r₁₂ added (`pl-tm`), its entries
--   numbers q₀ + q₁·ln 2 + q₂·π²; at g = 1 both are the old ones (`pl-agree`).
-- The certificate. A vector is x = p + q, p in the span, q orthogonal to it. With the 1s1s function e^{−2(r₁+r₂)} in
-- the span (α = 2, φ_000), q is orthogonal to the lowest state of H₀ = H_g − g/r₁₂, so ⟨q, H_g q⟩ ≥ ⟨q, H₀ q⟩ ≥
-- μ·⟨q, q⟩ with μ = −5/2, H₀'s next level (chem/tailblock.cub, `tb-he`). For λ < μ and c = μ − λ, completing the
-- square (chem/tailblock.cub, `tb-block`) gives c·⟨x, (H_g − λ)x⟩ ≥ pᵀ G(λ) p,
--   G(λ) = c·(Hm − λS) − (H2 − Hm S⁻¹ Hm),
-- since ‖Q H_g p‖² = pᵀ(H2 − Hm S⁻¹ Hm)p. So the level is at least λ when G(λ) is positive definite. No inverse is
-- computed: the 2n×2n block B(λ) = [[−S, Hm], [Hm, c·(Hm − λS) − H2]] has −S negative definite and G(λ) as the
-- complement of −S, so by Haynsworth's count it has n negative directions exactly when G(λ) has none: the verdict
-- is `wt-is n` on B(λ) (`pl-blk`). B is affine in (ln 2, π²), and a convex combination of positive definite G is
-- positive definite, so the four corners of a box holding (ln 2, π²) certify the true point (`pl-cert`; the box is
-- `pl-const`, from chem/he2.cub's enclosures). The upper end is Ritz's, the pencil (Hm, S) bracketed by
-- `wt-bracket`. The ends are found outside every proof (`pl-find`, `pl-ufind`); only the certificates are verdicts.
-- Taken here, not proved: the scaling; H_g ≥ H₀ for g ≥ 0 and H₀'s spectrum (its levels −2/n₁² − 2/n₂², 1s1s its
-- lowest state); Haynsworth's count for this block; Ritz's comparison; the passage from these matrix statements to
-- the operator on the function class.
import "he2.cub"
import "witness.cub"

